 "chapter": {
  "number": 143,
  "introduction": "CHAPT.CXLIII\n\nDavid complains and prays for pardon and help, ver. 1 - 12.\n\nA psalm of David.",
  "content": [
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 2,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "2. Justified - Upon terms of strict justice."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 3,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "3. For - This is not a reason of what he last said, but an argument to enforce his petition delivered, ver. 1. Soul - My life; nothing less will satisfy him. Dead - I am in as hopeless a condition in the eye of man, as those that have lain long in the grave."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 5,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "5. The days - What thou hast done for thy servants in former times."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 6,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "6. As land - Thirsteth for rain."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "verse",
    "number": 8,
    "content": [
     {
      "text": "Morning - Seasonably and speedily."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
